in @prism
in @meta
in @glass
in @magic
in @magic/contract
in @nl
in @epistemologic
in @epistemologic/cybernetic

# @magic/nl — the text-altitude adapter species. Bridges the @magic
# family (form/process at substrate altitude, #80) with the @nl family
# (raw unstructured natural language + Connes spectral primitives,
# per `shards/nl.mirror` Phase B lift) honestly via the adapter
# pattern, NOT decorative inheritance.
#
# Substrate-decl tick 2026-07-11 (post-fate-wiring landing).
# Operationalizes "@nl IS @magic at text altitude" the way
# @magic/frame (tick 23) operationalized "@frame IS @magic at
# cognitive altitude." Doubled-bilateral discipline; triple-carrier
# mapping.
#
# CRQ: how to discharge the "@nl IS @magic at text altitude"
# structural identity claim mechanically WITHOUT decorative
# inheritance (Seam C3, tick 7-10) and WITHOUT editing
# `shards/nl.mirror` (the family remains a floor + spectral
# primitives; the lift lives at adapter altitude)?
#
# Answer: the doubled-bilateral adapter pattern @magic/frame
# demonstrated. Take @nl carriers; MAP them to @magic carriers;
# declare a bilateral predicate that discharges BOTH family verdicts
# in one clause. Structural inheritance lives in the explicit map
# plus the doubled bilateral, not in an `in` clause that buys
# namespace ancestry without carrier flow.
#
# === The gauge-theoretic recognition (Reed grounding 2026-07-11) ===
#
# @magic at substrate altitude IS Yang-Mills gauge theory with a
# 5-op observable interface and matter-hidden mechanism (per
# magic.mirror lines 27-56). At text altitude the same shape is
# already operational:
#
#   text tokens (gauge-visible surface)         ↔ magic_surface
#   semantic content (matter-hidden meaning)    ↔ magic_mechanism
#   grammar / parse rules (invariant binding)   ↔ magic_invariant
#   language choice (cognitive frame)           ↔ @magic/frame
#   translation (atomic gauge swap)             ↔ @magic/reveal
#                                                 (forward-promised)
#
# The reader observes text (surface); semantic content is
# encapsulated behind Porter2 stemming + IDF weighting + the Dirac
# operator's spectral machinery (mechanism); grammar and parse rules
# bind the two via a named invariant. This adapter closes the
# surface / mechanism / invariant crossing at text altitude.
# Frame-crossing and reveal-crossing land at their respective
# adapters.
#
# === The adapter pattern (triple-carrier, per @magic/frame §2.2) ===
#
# Substrate-pull-correct mapping (triple-carrier, in @magic/frame's
# shape, not the single-carrier @magic/distinction shape):
#
#   nl (surface text)           ↔ magic_surface
#   spectral_triple (mechanism) ↔ magic_mechanism
#   corpus (invariant binding)  ↔ magic_invariant
#
# - Text-as-surface: `nl` is a content-addressed typed ref
#   (byte-equality). `magic_surface` is the same shape. Lift IS the
#   typed reframe.
# - Spectral-triple-as-mechanism: the (A, H, D) triple encapsulates
#   semantic content — token OID algebra, ℓ² Hilbert space, Dirac
#   operator all matter-side, hidden behind the corpus's opaque ref.
# - Corpus-as-invariant: Firth 1957: "you shall know a word by the
#   company it keeps." Meaning IS carried by the corpus, not by any
#   isolated token; the spectral triple's structure IS determined by
#   the corpus that constructed it.
#
# === The doubled-bilateral structural shape ===
#
# @magic/distinction (tick 15) discharges ONE parent-family predicate.
# @magic/frame (tick 23) discharges TWO. @magic/nl inherits the
# doubled shape:
#
#   1. `invariant_preserved` (@magic/contract line 163): boundary
#      harness at @io audits per recognition #57.
#   2. `nl_measurement_well_formed` (@nl family-root, per nl.mirror
#      lines 205-210): composed bilateral at @nl-measurement altitude;
#      corpus structurally valid for spectral triple construction
#      (non-empty vocabulary; IDF computed; Porter2-stemmed).
#
# Both must hold for the contract to satisfy @magic at text altitude.
# The signature takes a comparison corpus and a perturbation as
# explicit typed parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] because
# `nl_measurement_well_formed` is measurement-bilateral (needs two
# corpora); the single-contract lift extracts one corpus via the
# invariant field and the consumer names the second at the boundary.
#
# === Why this adapter does NOT edit `shards/nl.mirror` ===
#
# Adapter pattern per @magic/distinction and @magic/frame: decoration
# lives at adapter altitude. Parent family-root shard stays as-is.
# Consumers wanting @magic's discipline at text altitude route
# through this adapter; consumers wanting @nl alone route around it.
#
# === Pre-AI prior art ===
#
#   adapter pattern (GoF)       Gamma-Helm-Johnson-Vlissides 1994
#                               (*Design Patterns*). Inherited via
#                               @magic/distinction tick 15 and
#                               @magic/frame tick 23.
#   Yang-Mills gauge theory     Yang-Mills 1954. The physics ancestor
#                               of gauge-visible-with-matter-hidden.
#   Connes spectral triple      Connes 1985, 1994. The (A, H, D)
#                               structure @nl lifts to text altitude.
#   Firth distributional        Firth 1957 ("A synopsis of linguistic
#      hypothesis                theory"). Grounds corpus-as-invariant.
#
# === What this adapter does NOT do ===
#
# 1. Adapter is opt-in. Not every @nl is automatically a @magic.
# 2. Does NOT absorb @nl into @magic. Families remain distinct.
# 3. Does NOT edit `shards/nl.mirror`.
# 4. Does NOT discharge language-choice-as-frame (@magic/frame).
# 5. Does NOT discharge translation-as-gauge-swap (@magic/reveal,
#    forward-promised).
# 6. Does NOT lift `affect_profile` (species altitude).
#
# === Landing arc (cited by SHA) ===
#
# - b0427fd: @nl family-root Phase B lift (Connes spectral primitives).
# - 7e5c298: @docs.compose consumes @nl measurement.
# - f3af5b4: @optics/lens/features 16-dim graph_observation.
# - d9b7c35: Seam Adj 3 — the authority forward-promising this
#            adapter (fate-wiring landing's follow-on: Features::default()
#            v0 stub cmd_peer_beam lifts to real @nl-driven encoder
#            once @magic/nl is available).
#
# Once this lands: cmd_peer_beam v0's Features::default() can lift
# to a real @nl-driven encoder in a future Rust tick. Encoder invokes
# @nl to extract semantic-content-from-text (`ingest` + `build_triple`),
# @magic/nl to lift the spectral_triple to a magic_mechanism,
# @magic/contract.bind to compose surface+mechanism+invariant, then
# mosaic(feature) to structure into the 16-dim graph_observation.
# All existing substrate, no new families.
#
# Spec context: docs/specs/adapter-magic-frame-spec.md (adapter-
#               pattern precedent this shard inherits).
# Substrate decisions: [[architecture-shards-as-substrate-source]],
#                      [[architecture-prism-as-trait-as-everything]],
#                      [[architecture-form-process-partition-at-
#                       family-root]] (@magic form-side, @nl process-
#                       side; adapter threads them at text crossing),
#                      [[architecture-alignment-as-boundary-
#                       mathematics]] (#57; @io keeps surface/
#                       mechanism honest under lift),
#                      [[feedback-substrate-already-had-the-word]]
#                       (Firth + Connes + Yang-Mills + GoF),
#                      [[feedback-composition-claims-need-empirical-
#                       test]] (bilateral discharges "IS" empirically),
#                      [[feedback-no-bare-types]] (comparison corpus
#                       and perturbation typed).
# Related shards: magic.mirror (@magic family-root; form-side parent),
#                 nl.mirror (@nl family-root; text-altitude
#                  specialization; UNMODIFIED by this adapter),
#                 magic/distinction.mirror (single-bilateral adapter
#                  precedent, tick 15),
#                 magic/frame.mirror (doubled-bilateral adapter
#                  precedent, tick 23; this shard inherits its
#                  triple-carrier shape),
#                 magic/contract.mirror (consumer of the
#                  invariant_preserved predicate this adapter routes),
#                 magic/reveal.mirror (translation-as-gauge-swap
#                  composes here; forward-promised),
#                 optics/lens/features.mirror (the shard this unlocks
#                  v0→v1 for; Features::default() lifts to real
#                  @nl-driven encoder).
# Path-namespace property: this file at `shards/magic/nl.mirror`
# declares `@magic/nl` per `@epistemologic/pact/path_matches_namespace`.

source @arxiv/programming/gamma-helm-johnson-vlissides-1994
source @arxiv/physics/yang-mills-1954
source @arxiv/physics/connes-1994
source @arxiv/linguistics/firth-1957

prism @magic/nl {
  focus nl
  project nl
  split nl
  shift nl
  settle nl
}

# === text_as_surface adapter ===
#
# Substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting an @nl term to a
# @magic gauge-visible surface. Both are content-addressed typed
# refs with byte-equality identity; the lift IS the typed reframe.
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
text_as_surface(t: nl) -> magic_surface { \ }

# === triple_as_mechanism adapter ===
#
# Substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a spectral_triple to a
# @magic mechanism. The Connes (A, H, D) triple IS the matter-hidden
# mechanism giving text its spectral structure — token OID algebra,
# ℓ² Hilbert space, Dirac operator all matter-side, hidden behind
# the corpus's opaque `ref` identity. Encapsulation discipline
# inherited at @magic altitude (OID seal / parametric type / sheaf
# locality). Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
triple_as_mechanism(t: spectral_triple) -> magic_mechanism { \ }

# === corpus_as_invariant adapter ===
#
# Substrate-vocabulary adapter action lifting a corpus to a @magic
# named invariant. Corpus IS what binds surface and mechanism per
# Firth 1957. Splinter-pole: corpus honestly represents the text's
# provenance and the triple honestly preserves the corpus's spectral
# structure. Narcissus-pole: corpus is manipulated (cherry-picked,
# adversarially perturbed) to make surface text appear to satisfy
# the invariant while the underlying spectral distance fails; the
# boundary harness at @io audits the discrimination per #57.
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
corpus_as_invariant(c: corpus) -> magic_invariant { \ }

# === text_from_surface inverse adapter ===
#
# Type-relabeling inverse of `text_as_surface`, per @magic/frame §2.3
# (the `frame_from_surface` precedent): the inverse exists because
# both `nl` and `magic_surface` are typed refs with byte-equality
# identity. Round-trip identity (falsification check):
#   text_as_surface(text_from_surface(s)) = s
# for compatible surfaces. Failure = adapter mis-implemented.
# Body discharges at the realisation boundary.
text_from_surface(s: magic_surface) -> nl { \ }

# === nl_satisfies_magic bilateral predicate ===
#
# THE DOUBLED-BILATERAL cross-family predicate at text altitude.
# Substrate-pull-correct way to mechanically discharge the structural
# identity claim "@nl IS @magic at text altitude" without decorative
# inheritance.
#
# Two `requires` clauses, both load-bearing:
#
#   1. invariant_preserved(c, corpus_as_invariant(comparison_corpus))
#      — @magic/contract-family predicate. Discharges that the corpus
#      (lifted to magic_invariant) is preserved by the contract; the
#      boundary harness at @io audits this per recognition #57.
#
#   2. nl_measurement_well_formed(comparison_corpus, comparison_corpus,
#                                  perturbation)
#      — @nl-family composed bilateral (per shards/nl.mirror lines
#      205-210). Discharges that the corpus is structurally valid for
#      spectral triple construction. Measurement-side well-formedness.
#
# Both must hold for the contract to satisfy @magic at text altitude.
# The signature takes a comparison corpus and a perturbation as
# explicit typed parameters per [[feedback-no-bare-types]] because
# `nl_measurement_well_formed` is measurement-bilateral (needs two
# corpora); the single-contract lift extracts one corpus via the
# invariant field and the consumer names the second at the boundary.
#
# Consumer species (forward-promised @nl/english, @nl/markdown,
# @nl/german; the future Rust cmd_peer_beam v1 lifting
# Features::default() to real @nl-driven encoder per d9b7c35 Adj 3;
# alignment-at-text-altitude audits; spectral.engineer case-studies
# composing text-measurement with @magic-audit) name this predicate
# when their operation requires cross-family discharge.
nl_satisfies_magic(c: magic_contract, comparison_corpus: corpus, p: perturbation) -> verdict
requires invariant_preserved(c, corpus_as_invariant(comparison_corpus))
requires nl_measurement_well_formed(comparison_corpus, comparison_corpus, p)
{ \ }

# === Honest hedge per @magic/frame tick 28 review precedent ===
#
# Closed by this adapter:
#  - @nl term ↔ magic_surface round-trips via `text_as_surface` /
#    `text_from_surface`.
#  - spectral_triple ↔ magic_mechanism via `triple_as_mechanism`.
#  - corpus ↔ magic_invariant via `corpus_as_invariant`.
#  - Bilateral `nl_satisfies_magic` discharges BOTH family predicates
#    (invariant_preserved AND nl_measurement_well_formed).
#
# Not closed (forward-promised):
#  - Language-choice-as-frame (composes via @magic/frame's
#    `frame_as_surface`).
#  - Translation-as-gauge-swap (composes via @magic/reveal).
#  - affect_profile lift (species altitude).
#  - Round-trip identity at magic_contract-as-whole altitude (same
#    hedge @magic/frame preserved at tick 28: given magic_contract c,
#    `text_from_surface(c.surface)` DISCARDS c.mechanism and c.promise).

out @magic/nl
out text_as_surface
out triple_as_mechanism
out corpus_as_invariant
out text_from_surface
out nl_satisfies_magic
